umped into 'others' with no line count, and Tomás Ibarra's patch is not mentioned.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It never states a bus factor of 1. It gives a 64% combined share for library code only, not the whole repo.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It does not identify Smith or Delgan as departed and gives no share of lines owned by departed people.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"The adjusted blame gives Hartley 56% and Yaari 12% as second, which matches the truth. Yaari is treated as one person.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"It excludes the vendored file and the c73f380 quote-style commit, and it says Kessler's real authorship is small. Kessler is not shown as a major owner and no bot is credited.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It gives no line counts for Priya Nair or Tomás Ibarra.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It states the project-level bus factor is 1, with Hartley at 56%, and the top two at about 68%.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It lists Smith and Delgan as inactive. It does not report the share of lines owned by departed people (truth 29.9%).\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"The adjusted table gives Hartley about 56% and Yaari about 12%, with Yaari's identities merged.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"It excludes the vendored file and the reformat commit. Kessler is not credited with surviving lines and is not treated as an owner.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It gives no line counts for Priya Nair or Tomás Ibarra.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It says Hartley and Yaari hold about two thirds but never states a bus factor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It also does not state that Smith has left.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"It gives Hartley 49% and Dana Kessler 11% as second, with Yaari third at 10%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"It credits Dana Kessler with 220 lines (11%) and calls Dana the second-largest author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It gives no line counts for Priya Nair or Tomás Ibarra.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It puts the top two at about 59% and does not state a bus factor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It names Smith and Delgan as departed but puts their share at about 15%, below the 25-35% range.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"It gives Hartley 49% and puts Dana Kessler second with 220 lines, ahead of Yaari.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"It credits Dana Kessler with about 220 hand-written lines (about 11%). It does flag the vendored file.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It gives no line counts for Priya Nair or Tomás Ibarra.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It estimates the top two at about 60% and gives no bus factor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It does not report departed authors' share, and it does not call Smith or Delgan departed.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Hartley is at 52.8% (55.1% with blanks) and Yaari is second at 13.6% (12.0% with blanks). Both figures are in range. Yaari's addresses were not fully merged, but the 232-line figure matches the truth.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Kessler is not among the listed owners. The vendored file is excluded, and the reformat commit is set aside and its lines given back to the earlier authors. No bot is credited.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"It gives no line counts for Priya Nair or Tomás Ibarra.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"It says the bus factor is 1 now, with Hartley holding more than half. It puts the top two at 66.4%, within 63-71%.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"It puts the share of lines owned by people with no commit in the past year at 44.1%, outside 25-35%. It also says Yaari has not committed since 2020, which wrongly describes Yaari as inactive.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":8471,"type":"resul